From: mscharged-port
Subject: Use the inline GetOverlayManager body in the Striker Times overlay
Upstream-base: f75ccf1ad20e5bd7585962990db08067c0ae498a
Classification: native compiler compatibility; apply after 0643.

Retail fePopupMenu.cpp keeps an out-of-line copy of the inline
GetOverlayManager() from Game/GameInfo.inl. Native compilers inline it
everywhere and emit no copy, so OverlayHandlerStrikerTimes.cpp, which only sees
the plain declaration, left the game module with an unresolved symbol once 0642
admitted the overlay. Natively it includes the same inline body.

diff --git a/src/Game/FE/Overlay/OverlayHandlerStrikerTimes.cpp b/src/Game/FE/Overlay/OverlayHandlerStrikerTimes.cpp
index 97b95ce..5559d24 100644
--- a/src/Game/FE/Overlay/OverlayHandlerStrikerTimes.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/FE/Overlay/OverlayHandlerStrikerTimes.cpp
@@ -28,6 +28,10 @@
 #include "NL/nlPrint.h"
 #include "NL/nlString.h"
 #include "NL/nlFunction.inl"
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+// fePopupMenu.cpp owns the retail out-of-line copy, which native inlining drops.
+#include "Game/GameInfo.inl"
+#endif
 
 int gStrikerTimesCountdownSeconds = 10;
 
